    "title": "Program allows hunters to contribute deer meat to Ill. food pantries amid SNAP benefit freeze - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Rachel Grubbs ,\n5 hours ago ILLINOIS (KFVS) - Amid a delay in November Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program benefits, one effort aims to connect deer hunters with food pantries. According to the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign, Hunters Feeding Illinois allows hunters to donate their harvest for free to local meat processors, which then supply food pantries with venison. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 68",
